load ../ledger-freshness.maude

--- The round-trip scenario: evidence on d1 at h1, attested at c0; cut c1
--- edits d1 to h2; cut c2 undoes it back to h1; the frontier carries d1 at
--- h1 -- bit-identical to what was verified.

--- Coverage (the DR's defining fixture): edit-then-undo RESTORES freshness.
--- The verdict is a function of frontier content, not of the schedule.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, h2) u(c2, d1, h2, h1)
    bef(c0, c1) bef(c0, c2) bef(c1, c2) cur(d1, h1))
  =>* t(fresh C:Cfg) .

--- Bite: the round trip is never stale under content identity.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, h2) u(c2, d1, h2, h1)
    bef(c0, c1) bef(c0, c2) bef(c1, c2) cur(d1, h1))
  =>* t(stale(d1) C:Cfg) .

--- Bite: the round trip mints no witness either -- basis units after the
--- at-cut are not breaking cuts when the frontier still matches.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, h2) u(c2, d1, h2, h1)
    bef(c0, c1) bef(c0, c2) bef(c1, c2) cur(d1, h1))
  =>* t(wit(CU:CutId) C:Cfg) .

--- The genuine-edit scenario: cut c1 moves d1 from h1 to h2 and the frontier
--- carries h2.

--- Coverage: a real content change stales the entry.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, h2) bef(c0, c1) cur(d1, h2))
  =>* t(stale(d1) C:Cfg) .

--- Coverage (witness soundness, positive half): the stale verdict carries a
--- witness naming the breaking cut.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, h2) bef(c0, c1) cur(d1, h2))
  =>* t(stale(d1) wit(c1) C:Cfg) .

--- Bite: a mismatched basis never reads fresh.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, h2) bef(c0, c1) cur(d1, h2))
  =>* t(fresh C:Cfg) .

--- Bite (witness soundness, negative half): a post-attest unit on a
--- NON-basis identity (d2 is not in the fingerprint) is never a witness.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, h2) u(c2, d2, h1, h3)
    bef(c0, c1) bef(c0, c2) cur(d1, h2) cur(d2, h3))
  =>* t(wit(c2) C:Cfg) .

--- Coverage (purity): the same frontier with NO cut log at all is fresh.
--- Together with the round-trip search above this pins the purity claim --
--- same frontier, different histories, same verdict -- and merge stability
--- is structural: the state is an ACU set and the verdict a function of it,
--- so clones sharing events and frontier are literally the same term.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) cur(d1, h1))
  =>* t(fresh C:Cfg) .

--- The pure-rename scenario: cut c1 deletes d1 (which held h1) and adds d2
--- carrying the SAME canonical hash h1; the frontier has d2 at h1 and no d1.

--- Coverage: the entry is stale (its identity is gone) AND carries the
--- moved advisory pointing at the identity that now holds its content.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, nix) u(c1, d2, nix, h1)
    bef(c0, c1) cur(d2, h1))
  =>* t(stale(d1) moved(d1, d2) C:Cfg) .

--- The impure-rename scenario: same delete-plus-add shape in one cut, but
--- the added identity carries a DIFFERENT hash h2.

--- Bite: no moved advisory without canonical-hash equality at the frontier.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, nix) u(c1, d2, nix, h2)
    bef(c0, c1) cur(d2, h2))
  =>* t(moved(d1, I:Id) C:Cfg) .

--- Bite teeth: the SINCE-SCAN definition stales the round trip -- the exact
--- path-dependent verdict DR-0084 rejects, proving the good module's
--- round-trip No-solutions have real content.
search [1] in LEDGER-FRESHNESS-SINCE-SCAN :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, h2) u(c2, d1, h2, h1)
    bef(c0, c1) bef(c0, c2) bef(c1, c2) cur(d1, h1))
  =>* t(stale(d1) C:Cfg) .

--- Bite teeth: STRUCTURAL minting accepts the impure rename -- the same-cut
--- delete-plus-add shape mints moved despite the differing hash, proving the
--- good module's moved No-solution has real content.
search [1] in LEDGER-MOVED-STRUCTURAL :
  t(evd(d1, h1) att(c0) u(c1, d1, h1, nix) u(c1, d2, nix, h2)
    bef(c0, c1) cur(d2, h2))
  =>* t(moved(d1, d2) C:Cfg) .
